<title>GREECE: INTERNATIONAL LIFE TOPS 3-YR FIXED INCOME RETURNS.</title>
<headline>INTERNATIONAL LIFE TOPS 3-YR FIXED INCOME RETURNS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Life fixed income</p>
<p>fund topped all funds in its category with the best three-year</p>
<p>return from January 1 1994 to December 31 1996 -- 65.64 percent</p>
<p>-- Alpha Data &amp; Research said in a report on fixed income funds.</p>
<p>It ranked all fixed income mutual funds in Greece based on</p>
<p>returns during the three-year period assuming dividend</p>
<p>reinvestment on January 1 each year.</p>
<p>The rankings juxtapose fund performance with the average</p>
<p>12-month T-bill return during the same period and also indicate</p>
<p>the outperformance vis-a-vis T-bills.</p>
<p>The rankings have as follows:</p>
<p>    INCOME FUND	  RETURN   YEARLY  YEARLY T-BILL  OUTPERF</p>
<p>					   AVGE	AVGE</p>
<p>1. International Life  65.64%    21.88%    16.04%	  5.84%</p>
<p>2. Ergo		    64.81%    21.60%    16.04%	  5.57%</p>
<p>3. Vergina		 64.78%    21.59%    16.04%	  5.56%</p>
<p>4. Kosmos		  64.26%    21.42%    16.04%	  5.38%</p>
<p>5. ATE		     63.25%    21.08%    16.04%	  5.05%</p>
<p>6. Ionian Life	   63.04%    21.01%    16.04%	  4.98%</p>
<p>7. Delphi		  62.74%    20.91%    16.04%	  4.88%</p>
<p>8. European Reliance   62.62%    20.87%    16.04%	  4.84%</p>
<p>9. Natle Nederlanden   62.46%    20.82%    16.04%	  4.78%</p>
<p>10. Aspis		  61.45%    20.48%    16.04%	  4.45%</p>
<p>11. Delos		  61.18%    20.39%    16.04%	  4.36%</p>
<p>12. Alpha		  60.88%    20.29%    16.04%	  4.26%</p>
<p>13. Ionian		 60.54%    20.18%    16.04%	  4.26%</p>
<p>14. Interamerican	59.43%    19.81%    16.04%	  3.77%</p>
<p>15. Citifund	     58.01%    19.34%    16.04%	  3.30%</p>
<p>16. Dorian		 57.32%    19.11%    16.04%	  3.07%</p>
<p>17. Allianz		56.34%    18.78%    16.04%	  2.74%</p>
<p>18. Hermes		 56.22%    18.74%    16.04%	  2.70%</p>
<p>19. Midland		55.76%    18.59%    16.04%	  2.55%</p>
<p>20. Metrolife	    53.39%    18.46%    16.04%	  2.43%</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
